{% comment %}
  FAQ accordion. One block per question.

  Native <details>/<summary>: open and close, keyboard support, find-in-page
  and the accessibility tree all come free, and it still works with JS off.
  There is deliberately no JavaScript here.

  EVERY QUESTION IS CLOSED BY DEFAULT. The `open` setting stays, but nothing
  ships with it set.

  This reverses an earlier call to open the first one as a sample answer. A
  single expanded answer pushes the rest of the questions down the page --
  worst on a phone, where one long answer can be most of a screen -- so the
  reader sees fewer of the questions they came to scan. The scannable list is
  worth more than the demonstration.

  If one is ever opened again, open exactly one: an accordion with everything
  expanded is just a list.

  ELEMENT. The root is a <div>: `"tag": "section"` already wraps this.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="suf-section">
  <div class="suf-wrap">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        --head because this .suf-statement is a heading INSIDE a section
        rather than a section of its own. A standalone statement gets its
        space from the section padding below it and so zeroes its own bottom
        margin; here the accordion follows in the same section and there is no
        padding between the two.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="suf-statement suf-statement--head">
        <h2>{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.heading %}</h2>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="suf-faq">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- if block.settings.question != blank -%}
          <details {% if block.settings.open %}open{% endif %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <summary>{{ block.settings.question | escape }}</summary>
            <div class="suf-faq__answer">{% render 'suf-nb', text: block.settings.answer %}</div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "FAQ (SUF)",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 20,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Common Questions"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "question",
      "name": "Question",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "question", "label": "Question" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "answer", "label": "Answer" },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "open",
          "label": "Open by default",
          "info": "Leave off. If used, set it on one question only.",
          "default": false
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "FAQ (SUF)",
      "blocks": [{ "type": "question" }, { "type": "question" }]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
